  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 219 PM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nConvection already beginning to fire across western SD, approaching \nthe CWA. Any stronger cores that develop capable of strong wind \ngusts over 70 mph. Threat for severe weather still appears maximized \nover central SD late this afternoon into early evening. PoPs have \ncome in a little higher to around 50-70% early this evening. HRRR \ncontinues to be the more aggressive of the CAMs in regards to \nconvective areal coverage, but based on what's happening early this \nafternoon, it may be on to something. Will continue to monitor \nconvective trends and severe potential this afternoon and make \nchanges to messaging/forecast as necessary.\n\nAlso watching the high heat and humidity today. Central SD is \ncurrently in the low 100s air temperature, while conditions farther \neast are a bit cooler in the upper 80s to low 90s. Although, higher \ndewpoints over the east are pushing heat indices close to 100. Will \ncontinue the heat headlines with no changes as the advisory will \nextend into Sunday.",
